    "headline": "Can photography really save endangered species? National Geographic just shared a project that’s changing the game.",
    "challenge": "With biodiversity loss accelerating, many species are at risk of disappearing before we even know they exist. How can we raise awareness and inspire action?",
    "solution": "Joel Sartore’s Photo Ark project has documented over 18,000 species, showcasing their beauty and vulnerability to inspire conservation efforts. His stunning portraits are changing the way we see and value these creatures.",
    "resultHeading": "18,000+ species documented and counting",
    "resultLine": "The Photo Ark is over halfway to its goal of 25,000 species — explore the full archive at the link in bio.",
    "whyMatters": "The Photo Ark uses the power of photography to inspire people to protect at-risk species before it’s too late. By highlighting the beauty and vulnerability of these creatures, Sartore’s work reminds us of our shared responsibility to preserve Earth’s biodiversity.",
    "engagementQuestion": "What’s one endangered species you think more people should know about?",
